proposed_comments.body:
**[P2] Keep pending email HTML owned until publication (1/3)**

An item change cancels the old load and calls `Dispose`, but this load does not assign `_tempFile` until after the asynchronous write. Disposing while the write is pending can therefore see no owned file; the continuation can then assign a file after disposal. The write token is not a cleanup guarantee. Add shared lifetime state for the coordinated ownership fix below.

```suggestion
        private readonly DispatcherQueue _dispatcher;
        private readonly object _lifetimeLock = new();
        private bool _disposed;
```

**[P2] Clean unpublished email HTML on every exit (2/3)**

Keep the generated path locally owned until cancellation/disposal have been checked inside publication. A `finally` must delete the local path when writing, cancellation, or publication fails before ownership transfers. This also covers a partial file left by a cancelled write. Apply all three parts together.

```suggestion
            string? pendingTempFile = null;

            try
            {
                EmailMessage message = await Task.Run(
                    () => _file.Extension.Equals(".eml", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) ? EmlReader.Read(_file.Path) : MsgReader.Read(_file.Path),
                    cancellationToken);
                cancellationToken.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();

                Directory.CreateDirectory(TempFolderPath.Path);
                string tempFile = Path.Combine(TempFolderPath.Path, $"{Guid.NewGuid():N}.html");
                pendingTempFile = tempFile;
                await File.WriteAllTextAsync(tempFile, EmailHtmlRenderer.Render(message), cancellationToken);

                await _dispatcher.RunOnUiThread(() =>
                {
                    lock (_lifetimeLock)
                    {
                        cancellationToken.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();
                        ObjectDisposedException.ThrowIf(_disposed, this);
                        _tempFile = tempFile;
                        Preview = new Uri(tempFile);
                        pendingTempFile = null;
                    }
                });
            }
            catch (OperationCanceledException)
            {
                throw;
            }
            catch (Exception)
            {
                State = PreviewState.Error;
            }
            finally
            {
                if (pendingTempFile != null)
                {
                    DeleteTempFile(pendingTempFile);
                }
```

**[P2] Prevent ownership transfer after disposal (3/3)**

Use the same lock for disposal and publication so an earlier `Dispose` cannot be followed by a new ownership transfer. Capture and clear the owned path before best-effort deletion. Verify cancellation/navigation during an email HTML write leaves no abandoned file, while an ordinary successful preview remains available until disposal. Apply all three parts together.

```suggestion
            string? tempFile;
            lock (_lifetimeLock)
            {
                _disposed = true;
                tempFile = _tempFile;
                _tempFile = null;
            }

            if (tempFile != null)
            {
                DeleteTempFile(tempFile);
            }

            GC.SuppressFinalize(this);
        }

        private static void DeleteTempFile(string tempFile)
        {
            try
            {
                File.Delete(tempFile);
            }
            catch (IOException)
            {
            }
            catch (UnauthorizedAccessException)
            {
            }
```
